<BaseLayout title="A/C System" description="A/C retention, wiring, and hose routing for LS Genesis Coupe swaps.">
  <h1>A/C System</h1>
  <p>
    Wire colors for A/C request vary by year. Verify with power on and the A/C button pressed (12V and/or continuity at the cabin plug).
  </p>

  <img src="/images/ac-cabin-plug.jpg" alt="A/C control module plug in cabin with AC pins marked" />
  <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: -0.5rem;">
    Plug to the A/C controls in the cabin — marked pins are the A/C request/control wires to verify with power on.
  </p>

  <img src="/images/ac-wires-on.jpg" alt="Yellow and blue A/C wires at passenger side connectors" />
  <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: -0.5rem;">
    Yellow and blue wires at the passenger-side connectors — these are the A/C-on signals on many years (confirm on your car).
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>2010 2.0T example:</strong> Yellow (Pin 21 A/C select high) and Blue (Pin 22 A/C output high) on the A/C control module; same colors on the smaller passenger fuse-box plug.</li>
    <li><strong>2013 3.8:</strong> Same colors (yellow and blue) on the larger plug leading to the passenger-side fuse box.</li>
  </ul>

  <img src="/images/ac-2013-38-larger-plug.jpg" alt="2013 3.8 larger plug to passenger fuse box with yellow and blue A/C wires marked" />
  <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: -0.5rem;">
    2013 3.8 — larger plug to the passenger-side fuse box. Yellow and blue are the A/C wires.
  </p>

  <p>
    To keep stock A/C function: retain the fuse-box harness and ECU (you can still trim unused engine-control wires). Many hide the fuse box under a relocated battery.
  </p>
  <p>
    Holley Terminator X path often uses the Current Performance Holley A/C add-on module harness, a Vintage Air 11079-VUS binary switch, and the matching pigtail.
    Low-mount F-body Holley A/C bracket setups are common; stock A/C hoses usually need to be shortened/re-ended at a hose shop.
  </p>

  <img src="/images/ac-engine-bay-overview.jpg" alt="LS swapped red Genesis Coupe engine bay showing A/C compressor and hose routing" />
  <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: -0.5rem;">
    Overall bay view — low-mount A/C compressor on the passenger side with custom hose routing.
  </p>

  <img src="/images/ac-compressor-closeup.jpg" alt="Close-up of A/C compressor fittings and hard lines" />
  <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: -0.5rem;">
    Compressor fittings and hard-line connections.
  </p>

  <img src="/images/ac-compressor-clutch-hoses.jpg" alt="A/C compressor clutch and PolarSeal hose routing" />
  <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: -0.5rem;">
    Clutch and hose routing clear of the accessory drive.
  </p>

